# Where the vendored web module came from.
#
# app.py, static/, tests/, install.sh, uninstall.sh and systemd/ were copied
# from the vps-webserver repository at the tag below, then adapted: the
# environment prefix VPSWS_ became VPSSRV_, VPSWS_PORT split into
# VPSSRV_CONSOLE_PORT (80/443 now belong to the public page), the HTTP-to-HTTPS
# redirect listener was removed, Handler became ConsoleHandler, and
# ProbeHandler plus the iperf3 window were added.
#
# Refreshing this vendored tree means re-copying from a newer upstream tag and
# updating this file in the SAME commit. Never hand-edit vendored code without
# recording it here — a local change that upstream does not know about turns
# the next refresh into a silent regression.

vps-webserver v0.4.1
